  "worked_solution": "The number is *negative* because it is to the *left* of zero.\n\nThe absolute value of the number is $\\frac{19}{6},$ so the distance between that number and zero on a number line is $\\frac{19}{6}.$ \n\nThe negative number at a distance of $\\frac{19}{6}$ from zero is $-\\frac{19}{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14145654/assets/9a78acce2ae81830a505b53a9b5ea2d44c113fc49f733e86a2e064f5683f3f9b.png)",
